{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.215,
   "text": "The old arcade on the boardwalk has a photo booth in the back corner."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.815,
   "end": 15.407,
   "text": "The owner had one rule for whoever closes up: once the boardwalk lights go out, never sit in that booth."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.107,
   "end": 18.347,
   "text": "All summer, I never did."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 19.347,
   "end": 25.96,
   "text": "Then, on the last night of the season, the lights went dark... and behind me, the booth started up on its own."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.76,
   "end": 29.021,
   "text": "Flash. Flash. Flash."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.621,
   "end": 35.741,
   "text": "Nobody was inside. But the curtain was swaying, like someone had just stood up."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.441,
   "end": 39.705,
   "text": "A strip of photos dropped into the tray."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.905,
   "end": 46.751,
   "text": "Three pictures of the empty seat... and in each one, the curtain was pulled open a little wider."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 47.451,
   "end": 51.141,
   "text": "In the last one, a pale hand was holding it open."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.541,
   "end": 57.915,
   "text": "I left the keys on the counter and walked home without looking back."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.915,
   "end": 64.525,
   "text": "It wasn't until I got into bed that I remembered... that booth always prints four pictures."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.125,
   "end": 69.432,
   "text": "This morning, the fourth one was on my pillow."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.632,
   "end": 74.515,
   "text": "It was me, asleep... taken from right beside my bed."
  }
 ],
